<?xml version="1.0"?>
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
      xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <!--
            Renderer one: the card template.

            `product_list_item` is the block Hyvä renders every card through — see
            `Hyva\Theme\ViewModel\ProductListItem::getItemHtml()`, which looks the block up by that
            exact name. Repointing its template is the whole integration: category listings, search
            results, the compare page and Hyvä's own product slider all reach the card through this
            one block, so none of them needs its own hook.

            It is also, honestly, a fork of Hyvä's `product/list/item.phtml`. The template it
            replaces reproduces Hyvä's structure deliberately (same form, same child blocks, same
            order) so third-party injections keep working, and the README says what to re-check
            after a Hyvä upgrade. Delete this one file to go back to the stock card — the ViewModel
            layer, the GraphQL fields and the minicart plugins are unaffected.
        -->
        <referenceBlock name="product_list_item" template="Scr1be_HyvaProductCard::product/list/card.phtml"/>
    </body>
</page>
